<div class="header-box">
    <h1 style="margin-top: 0; border-bottom: none; padding-bottom: 0;">Studds QC Bluetooth Device Inspection Application</h1>
    <h3 style="margin-top: 4pt; color: #1e40af;">Technical Specification Document (TS) — Detailed Line-by-Line Guide</h3>
    <p style="margin-bottom: 0;"><strong>Document ID:</strong> STUDDS-QC-TS-DETAILED-V1.0 &nbsp;|&nbsp; <strong>Date:</strong> 2026-08-26 &nbsp;|&nbsp; <strong>Target Platform:</strong> Windows 10 / 11 (64-bit)</p>
    <p style="margin-bottom: 0;"><strong>Author:</strong> Studds Software Engineering & QA Architecture Team &nbsp;|&nbsp; <strong>Status:</strong> Approved & Production Baseline</p>
</div>

<div class="alert-box">
    <h4 style="margin-top: 0; color: #854d0e;">📖 Note for Non-Technical Stakeholders & Reviewers:</h4>
    <p style="margin-bottom: 0;">This document is written in <strong>simple, plain English</strong>. You do not need a computer science degree or programming experience to understand how this system works. Every file, function, and configuration block is explained with real-world analogies, plain English breakdowns, and exact <strong>"How to Change This"</strong> step-by-step recipes so anyone can modify application settings (like database passwords, test voice phrases, audio tracks, or window sizes) safely.</p>
</div>

<h2>1. System Architecture in Simple Terms</h2>

<p>Think of the application like a restaurant with 3 main parts:</p>

<table style="width: 100%;">
    <tr>
        <th style="width: 30%;">Component</th>
        <th style="width: 30%;">Technical Name</th>
        <th>Plain English Purpose & What It Does</th>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td><strong>1. The Frontend UI</strong><br><em>(The Dining Room)</em></td>
        <td><code>studds_qc_inspection.html</code><br>(PyWebView Edge Chromium)</td>
        <td>What the inspector sees on screen (buttons, progress bars, volume meters, pass/fail badges). Runs in a smooth native desktop window.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td><strong>2. The Backend Engine</strong><br><em>(The Kitchen & Chef)</em></td>
        <td><code>qc_bluetooth_api.py</code><br>(FastAPI on Port 8765)</td>
        <td>Takes commands from the screen, controls the computer's Bluetooth radio, plays speaker sound files, listens to the microphone, and checks physical buttons.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td><strong>3. The Central Database</strong><br><em>(The Filing Cabinet)</em></td>
        <td>MySQL / MariaDB Server<br>(Table: <code>inspection_logs</code>)</td>
        <td>Stores records of every single helmet tested: Operator ID, Serial Number, MAC Address, Date, Time, and PASS/FAIL verdict.</td>
    </tr>
</table>

